--- a/docs/changelog.md
+++ b/docs/changelog.md
@@ -12,6 +12,14 @@ See the [Contributing Guide](contributing.md) for details.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+* Footnotes are now numbered and ordered by the order in which they are first
+  referenced in the document rather than the order in which they are defined.
+  A new configuration option for the footnotes extension, `USE_DEFINITION_ORDER`,
+  has been added to restore the previous behavior of ordering footnotes by the
+  order of their definitions.
+
 ### Fixed
 
 * Fix handling of incomplete HTML tags in code spans in Python 3.14.
diff --git a/docs/extensions/footnotes.md b/docs/extensions/footnotes.md
index e841a32..d4b4d6d 100644
--- a/docs/extensions/footnotes.md
+++ b/docs/extensions/footnotes.md
@@ -98,6 +98,18 @@ The following options are provided to configure the output:
 * **`SEPARATOR`**:
     The text string used to set the footnote separator. Defaults to `:`.
 
+* **`USE_DEFINITION_ORDER`**:
+    Whether to order footnotes by the order in which they are defined in the
+    document rather than by the order in which they are first referenced.
+    Defaults to `False`.
+
+    By default, footnotes are numbered and listed in the order in which they are
+    first referenced in the document. Footnotes which are only referenced from
+    within other footnotes follow those referenced in the body of the document, and
+    any footnotes which are never referenced are listed last in the order they were
+    defined. Set this option to `True` to restore the behavior of versions prior to
+    3.9, where footnotes were ordered by the order of their definitions.
+
 A trivial example:
 
 ```python
